Package: LeafInjuryR
Type: Package
Title: Quantification of Visual Leaf Injury Patterns from Digital Images
Version: 0.2.1
Date: 2026-10-18
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = c("Wilhan", "Valasco"),
        family = "dos Santos",
        email = "wilhanvalasco@hotmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")
    )
Description: Provides an image-processing workflow for quantifying visual
    leaf injury from digital RGB photographs. The workflow includes
    leaf-background segmentation, classification of healthy and injured
    leaf tissues, and estimation of injured area as a percentage of total
    leaf area. Tissue classification supports binary categories
    (healthy and injured) and optional multiclass categories
    (healthy, chlorotic, necrotic, and other). Six public functions
    support image cropping, automatic and manually corrected segmentation,
    individual and batch analyses, validation against manually generated
    reference masks, and a local interactive interface implemented with
    'shiny'. Validation metrics include intersection over union, Dice
    coefficient, sensitivity, specificity, precision, and F1 score.
    Batch analyses generate HTML reports, Excel workbooks, and CSV tables,
    with processing parameters recorded to support reproducibility.
    The package quantifies visible injury patterns but does not diagnose
    pathogens, diseases, nutritional disorders, or phytotoxicity.
    All image processing is performed locally.
